From a71cb3a92c59525b864eef0271c3a9a488bc8fb6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:35:28 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/31] kcm_keys: component list filled off the first frame,
 Add first in the toolbar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: List with a detail pane (docs/page-design.md section 1; the two panes stay because the user compares and
edits many components in a row, and one search field above the list is the fastest route). KGlobalAccel actions,
key sequences, scheme files (.kksrc), command .desktop files and all D-Bus calls are unchanged.

Moved / renamed (kcm_keys/AddNew, Import, Export):
- Toolbar order by use: "Add New" -> "Add…" (Application…, Command or Script…) first, then "Import Scheme…" and
  "Export Scheme…" (were "Import…", "Export…").
- Search field says "Search shortcuts…"; the empty states carry an icon; busy indicator after 150 ms.
- Section titles (Applications, Commands, System Services, Common Actions) already are nouns: kept.
- Per ia/duplicates.md: this page stays the full editor. Zoom/Magnifier, Activity and Keyboard Layout shortcuts are
  owned by their context pages (kcm_access, kcm_activities, kcm_keyboard) and still show here.
- Relabel table: inventory/relabel/kcm_keys.tsv (outer repo). Inventory --strict: 25 rows ok, 0 lost (markers
  "ksr: kcm_keys/..." added next to every text-only control).

Speed (cause from code, not measured):
- KCMKeys::load() ran StandardShortcutsModel::load() synchronously (about 80 KStandardShortcut lookups plus
  QCollator sorts of every category and action list) before the first frame; it now runs one event-loop turn later.
- GlobalAccelModel::loadComponent() ran per KGlobalAccel component inside the D-Bus reply handlers: KService lookup,
  and for every component without a desktop file (kwin, plasmashell, kded modules, ...) a full
  KApplicationTrader::query() over all installed applications, plus a new QCollator per component. Now the replies
  only collect the infos; components are built one per event-loop turn, the application list is queried once per
  load into a name hash (same "first match" result), one collator is shared, and the model is still reset once at
  the end (the krunner keys runner relies on that). A generation counter drops stale loads; an empty component list
  now also ends loading (it never reset the model before).
- Numbers: before (build/bench/clean/before-slow.tsv) among the slowest pages. After: pending, manager will measure.

HIG: HIG-001, HIG-005, HIG-006, HIG-019, HIG-047, HIG-058.

Not built yet (freeze).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
